<header class="sp-head"><p class="featured-region">15 February 1819 · Angostura, Venezuela</p><h1 class="sp-title">Bolívar at Angostura</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>In the middle of the wars for South American independence, Simón Bolívar opened a congress at Angostura on the Orinoco and set out his vision for the government of the free republics.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>Key passage</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>Unity, unity, unity must be our motto.</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">Address to the Congress of Angostura, 1819.</p><div class="sp-full"><a class="sp-full-link" href="https://es.wikisource.org/wiki/Discurso_de_Sim%C3%B3n_Bol%C3%ADvar_ante_el_Congreso_de_Angostura" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the complete text<span aria-hidden="true"> &#8599;</span></a><span class="sp-full-src">Spanish original, Wikisource</span></div></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>The congress named Bolívar president and prepared the republic of Gran Colombia, proclaimed that year. Gran Colombia broke apart in 1831, the year after Bolívar's death, into Venezuela, Colombia and Ecuador.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-boyaca">Battle of Boyacá</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carabobo">Battle of Carabobo</a></div></div></section>
